{"id": "EUVD-2026-86639", "enisaUuid": "eee98fbd-3518-31e6-85ac-27fa02802c6b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\naf_unix: Update last skb marker in manage_oob().\n\nFahad Alharbi reported that blocking recv(MSG_PEEK) could hog CPU\ndue to OOB skb.\n\nIn the following cases, manage_oob() skips OOB skb(s) and returns\nNULL for the last recv(MSG_PEEK):\n\n  socketpair(AF_UNIX, SOCK_STREAM, 0, sk);\n\n  1) skb -> OOB skb -> NULL\n     send(sk[0], \"ab\", 2, MSG_OOB);\n     recv(sk[1], buf, 0, MSG_PEEK);\n\n  2) skb -> consumed OOB skb -> NULL\n     send(sk[0], \"ab\", 2, MSG_OOB);\n     recv(sk[1], buf, 1, MSG_OOB);\n     recv(sk[1], buf, 0, MSG_PEEK);\n\n  3) consumed OOB skb -> OOB skb -> NULL\n     send(sk[0], \"a\", 1, MSG_OOB);\n     recv(sk[1], buf, 0, MSG_OOB);\n     send(sk[0], \"b\", 1, MSG_OOB);\n     recv(sk[1], buf, 1, MSG_PEEK);\n\nThen, @copied is 0 in unix_stream_read_generic() (zero-length buffer,\nor non-OOB skb is not yet consumed), and unix_stream_data_wait() is\ncalled.\n\nHowever, it returns immediately because @last is not updated in\nunix_stream_read_generic(), and the thread busy-waits for a new skb.\n\nLet's update @last in manage_oob().\n\nFor MSG_PEEK, @last is updated with the skipped OOB, and for the\nnon-peek case, @last matches the returned value (when !copied)\nbecause OOB is unlinked.\n\nNote that manage_oob() is inlined and no stack canary is added.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:53:57", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bd91dc313afe21e9d6b31ca6a47606a33ca5e35c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0630bfc773d85ac44da05b2c5a037dbbd39301ab", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f1816b3d7ce80dcf086bb68ff5ae6e09520ca1fa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fc62a26493a98a0424d9dae2eb92a1daa1321f65", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/94fd4debd2e3a69cf93e766c8b328a810c228119"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97985", "GHSA-cq66-2f6w-rhg5"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "073ad071-4502-3cd1-b2a7-b906a0020b16", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22dd70eb2c3d754862964377a75abafd3167346b <f1816b3d7ce80dcf086bb68ff5ae6e09520ca1fa"}, {"id": "189f9f16-eaab-306b-a361-be875b8c411a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "1a0df43a-624b-350a-b666-db6939aff14e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8.8 <6.9"}, {"id": "1af20366-2912-329a-be6d-ee6c28a19d14", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "1da76760-13ff-3808-9f58-6d8616ca2f5c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22dd70eb2c3d754862964377a75abafd3167346b <fc62a26493a98a0424d9dae2eb92a1daa1321f65"}, {"id": "2e72b7c6-5483-36fe-b903-01716e885dd6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae3f9e1221b31b18dbd4c4b85d08574996bbd973"}, {"id": "35749014-8492-3ae6-a33a-fc619dcd00e1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22dd70eb2c3d754862964377a75abafd3167346b <0630bfc773d85ac44da05b2c5a037dbbd39301ab"}, {"id": "4e32144f-e861-33ea-8e2a-cda089df54ec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ba0db4638525b8b054b3d546b45f7e473f477027"}, {"id": "71854a86-d8a4-38cb-8fa8-64faaf96eccb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "9d0ceb9a-8461-32f2-a75d-cd84992e698b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a3a58cd2-f140-33cf-b5bc-9179a598f768", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "b2ae6dd3-17e7-3c21-83b8-9ed6365816f7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_v